{"Title":"An Act relative to the workers’ compensation premium payment schedules for small businesses","BillNumber":"S695","DocketNumber":"SD1777","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"SLM0","Name":"Susan L. Moran","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/SLM0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T10:21:29.253"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"SLM0","Name":"Susan L. Moran","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/SLM0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T10:21:29.2533333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S695/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Ms. Moran, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 695) of Susan L. Moran for legislation relative to the workers’ compensation premium payment schedules for small businesses.  Financial Services.","DocumentText":"\tSection 25Q of Chapter 152 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended in subsection (4) by adding, after the first sentence, the following sentence:- \r\n\tSubsection (1) shall not apply to groups that have been in existence for at least 5 years and have established a premium payment plan acceptable to the commissioner. \r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J11","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J11"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}